The scope is every two-digit month `00..99`, every two-digit day `00..99`, and
years `0000`, `2000`, `2023`, and `9999`, plus 12 malformed/Unicode cases.
This is finite evidence, not a universal equivalence proof.

# Excluded behavior

- non-string arguments;
- Python exceptions and behavior outside the supplied MPY subset;
- leap-year validation or a numeric year range, neither requested by the
  prompt;
- claims about termination beyond the Kit's partial-correctness interpretation;
- correctness of the K implementation, supplied semantics, or translator
  themselves beyond the named trust boundary;
- retained module-scope contents after the returned Boolean, which are
  unobservable in the function contract.
